- DEVIATION from mission text (evidence-based, recorded): cmdline gains ONLY " adreno_only=1", not " adreno_fine=1".
  Reasons: (a) wave23 ground truth -- the 607 budget is the COMBINED line: loader prepends a 110-char header
  (debug=0x8 / rd=md0 / ufs_shared_pa / hakios_kver), payload cmdline goes LAST and is TRUNCATED past 607
  (loader.c:3617-3625 prints a WARNING). Budget for the payload cmdline = 607-110 = 497 chars; v26 uses 477
  (spare 20). " adreno_only=1" (14) -> 491 fits; " adreno_fine=1" would make 505 -> the tail of exactly that
  arg gets cut. (b) under the gpu=1 path pause_ms=0, and hold() no-ops on pause_ms==0 regardless of fine --
  adreno_fine is inert unless paired with adreno_pause; localization comes from the newest_step=1 prints,
  which adreno_only=1 alone provides. Hang evidence survives (loader notes the log end every 2 s from
  another core; the hang is indefinite, zero panic per v26 gen1).
- fix-direction recon done while building (no device touch): kodiak (sm8475) gcc = refs gcc-waipio.c
  (that is why wave36's grep for gcc-sm8475.c missed). GPU offsets differ from the sc7280 values the
  driver carries:
    clock            driver now (sc7280)   kodiak waipio
    GCC_PLL_VOTE     0x52000               0x62000
    gpu_cfg_ahb      0x71004               0x81004
    gpu_memnoc_gfx   0x7100c               0x81010
    gpu_snoc_dvm     0x71018               0x81018
    ddrss_gpu_axi    0x71154               0x81154
  NOTE: kodiak offsets reach 0x81xxx > the driver's gcc mapping size 0x80000 -> the fix must also widen
  the mapping (waipio DTB reg = 0x1f7220). Evidence first: v27 probe decides; no fix before the hang line.

